    "preFilingReview": "TWO-STAGE STRUCTURE. Stage 1 (sponsorship): chief petitioners file form SEL 310, Prospective Petition for State Measure, then gather 1,000 sponsorship signatures on Elections Division-issued sponsorship templates. The Division verifies them; if the petition falls short, chief petitioners get exactly one more submission to reach 1,000, after which the petition is void. Reaching 1,000 valid sponsorship signatures triggers the ballot title process: the Attorney General files a draft ballot title, any registered voter may file written comments, the Secretary of State separately conducts a Procedural Constitutional Review (single subject / full text / legislative-not-administrative, plus the separate-vote and amend-not-revise tests for constitutional measures), and the Attorney General then issues a certified ballot title. A voter who filed comments and is dissatisfied may petition the Oregon Supreme Court for review within 10 business days of certification. Stage 2 (full circulation): only after the ballot title is final, the Division approves the cover and signature sheets, and chief petitioners have reviewed circulation requirements with their circulators, may general signature gathering begin. Signatures gathered on approved sheets are filed monthly. Approval to circulate for a cycle is not granted until after the prior cycle's signature deadline (the 2026 cycle opened July 8, 2024), and only one petition cycle is approved for circulation in any two-year period.",
