      "Texas has no statewide initiative, no statewide veto referendum and no citizen route to a constitutional amendment. Only the Legislature may propose an amendment (two-thirds of each chamber in a single session), which voters then approve by simple majority. Voters rejected a proposed initiative-and-referendum amendment in 1914 and it has not been revived. All statewide initiative fields are null because the mechanism does not exist, not because a number could not be found.",
